\ save-system-native.4 - SAVE-SYSTEM for the native kernel (docs/NATIVE.md
\ section 10, Iteration 638). Loaded after save-system.4 when the native
\ shell is built (tools/build-native-shell.sh); save-system.4 itself is
\ shared with CV8 and stays as it is - its helpers are used here.
\ The same steps as save-system.4's: the pool's buffers released, START
\ to HERE copied, DP and every word list's thread heads made offsets again
\ in the copy - COLD adds START to them at each boot - and the scratch
\ cells blanked, so two saves of one system are the same. Then, where
\ save-system.4 writes CV8's header, the native image's own: the ELF
\ header page, mapped just below START (native-cross.4's segment begins
\ there), with the file's size made this image's; the entry and the
\ memory's size stay - the start is the kernel's, inside the image.
CREATE SSN-HDR 4096 ALLOT
: SSN-UNRELOCATE-ALL ( --- )
  DP SS-UNRELOCATE
  FORTH-WORDLIST SS-UNRELOCATE-WORDLIST
  WORDLISTS @
  BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    START @ + DUP SS-UNRELOCATE-WORDLIST
    1 CELLS - @
  REPEAT ;
: SSN-DATA-AT ( --- u )   SS-LEN @ 4096 + 4095 + -4096 AND ;   \ the data's place in the file
: SSN-HEADER ( --- )   \ the running image's header page, its p_filesz this image's
  START @ 4096 - SSN-HDR 4096 MOVE
  SS-LEN @ 4096 +  SSN-HDR 96 + !
  SSN-DATA-AT SSN-HDR 128 + !  DDP @ DATA-BASE -  SSN-HDR 152 + ! ;   \ (672) the data's
: SAVE-SYSTEM ( c-addr u --- )
  RESET-BUFFERS  DATA-OFF
  HERE START @ - SS-LEN !
  \ (674) the copy runs from START to data's end - the code, the room
  \ between, the data - so SS>COPY, START-relative, finds the kernel's
  \ own variables in it where they live now, in data's region
  DDP @ START @ - ALLOCATE ABORT" SAVE-SYSTEM: out of memory" SS-BUF !
  START @ SS-BUF @ DDP @ START @ - MOVE
  SSN-UNRELOCATE-ALL
  SS-SCRUB
  SSN-HEADER
  W/O BIN CREATE-FILE ABORT" SAVE-SYSTEM: cannot create file" SS-FID !
  SSN-HDR 4096 SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP
  SS-BUF @ SS-LEN @ SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP
  SSN-HDR 4096 0 FILL  SSN-HDR  SSN-DATA-AT SS-LEN @ 4096 + -  SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP
  SS-BUF @ DATA-BASE START @ - +  DDP @ DATA-BASE -  SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP   \ (672, 674) data's
  SS-FID @ CLOSE-FILE DROP
  SS-BUF @ FREE DROP ;
